From: Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] devtools-frontend: run the JS tsc, not the prebuilt tsgo ELF

Every devtools TypeScript step in M155 runs `tsc_binary` from
scripts/build/typescript/typescript_vars.gni: the .d.ts and the -p
compile in typescript.gni, and the check in ts_type_check.gni.  It names
the prebuilt tsgo under //third_party/typescript/linux-amd64/src/lib/tsc
and lists it as a ninja input.  That directory is not in keeplibs, so the
tree ships it empty and ninja dies before running anything:

  ninja: error: '../../third_party/typescript/linux-amd64/src/lib/tsc',
  needed by 'gen/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/front_end/...d.ts', missing
  and no known rule to make it

Point the Linux branch at the JS compiler devtools vendors in its own
node_modules (TypeScript 6.0.2 in M155).  bin/tsc is executable with a
`#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang, so run_with_restat.py and run_with_stamp.py
can exec it as-is, and it accepts every flag the build passes
(--ignoreConfig, --noCheck, --noResolve, ...).  This also removes the last
amd64-only binary from the devtools build.  The lib.*.d.ts list next to it
is only added to the inputs under use_remoteexec, so it needs no change.

One flag has to go: the .d.ts step passes --isolatedDeclarations, which
TypeScript 6 enforces more strictly than tsgo (TypeScript 7) -- it rejects
optional parameter properties such as
core/host/DispatchHttpRequestClient.ts's `readonly response?: ...` with
TS9025.  The flag only validates that declarations are derivable per file;
emission does not depend on it, and upstream already enforces the property
with tsgo on every change.

Rebase of chromium-154-devtools-tsc-binary-via-node.patch: M155 folded
ts_library_split.gni into typescript.gni and deleted ts_library.py, which
also retired chromium-153-devtools-tsc-via-node.patch -- no Python path to
tsgo is left in the build (only extensions/cxx_debugging/e2e/runner.py,
a test runner).

Goes together with the gn arg use_typescript_go=false.  Drop both once the
tree ships a tsgo that survives unbundling, or devtools regains a node
fallback.
--- a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/scripts/build/typescript/typescript.gni
+++ b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/scripts/build/typescript/typescript.gni
@@ -298,7 +298,12 @@
           "--ignoreConfig",
           "--declaration",
           "--emitDeclarationOnly",
-          "--isolatedDeclarations",
+
+          # bentoo: --isolatedDeclarations only *validates* that each file's
+          # declarations can be emitted in isolation; it does not change the
+          # emitted .d.ts. The JS tsc (TypeScript 6) rejects optional parameter
+          # properties under it (TS9025) where tsgo (TypeScript 7) accepts
+          # them, e.g. core/host/DispatchHttpRequestClient.ts.
           "--noCheck",
           "--noResolve",
           "--outDir",
--- a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/scripts/build/typescript/typescript_vars.gni
+++ b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/scripts/build/typescript/typescript_vars.gni
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@
 import("../ninja/vars.gni")
 
 if (host_os == "linux") {
-  tsc_binary = "//third_party/typescript/linux-amd64/src/lib/tsc"
+  # bentoo: the JS compiler from devtools' own node_modules, not the prebuilt
+  # tsgo ELF, which is stripped from the tree and has no arm64 build.
+  tsc_binary = devtools_location_prepend + "node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc"
 } else if (host_os == "win") {
   tsc_binary = "//third_party/typescript/windows-amd64/src/lib/tsc.exe"
 } else if (host_os == "mac") {
